							"documentation": "setVariable() stores the value in the variable's slot. evaluate() runs the Program built with the expression: generated bytecode (BYTECODE) or the CompiledExpression interpreter (INTERPRETED, or when classes cannot be defined at runtime). Both read the variable slots, compute built-ins with Builtins and call apply(double...) only on custom functions and operators. A malformed expression has no Program: its tokens are interpreted on an ArrayStack so that the original error is reported.",
							"ownedElements": [
								{
									"_type": "UMLSequenceDiagram",
									"_id": "9rYZG5eOXaZ4CJAXI3UA",
									"_parent": {
